msgid "GB125_Saladin_LS_BOT"
msgstr "Detonator"

msgid "GB125_Saladin_LS_BOT_descr"
msgstr ""
"The FV601 Saladin wheeled armored vehicle, designed by Alvis Car and "
"Engineering Company, was meant to replace the AEC Armoured Car. Work started"
" in 1946, but the practical stage did not begin until the first half of the "
"1950s. The vehicle's distinctive features were its chassis with 6x6 wheel "
"configuration and its outrigger suspension. The first two prototypes of the "
"FV 601 (B) were produced in 1955. Two years later, a total of six pilot "
"armored vehicles were built, and in 1958, mass production was launched. The "
"armored vehicle was produced until 1972, most often in the Saladin Mk. 2 "
"modification. A total of 1,177 vehicles were built. The vehicle was actively"
" used in the Middle East and Africa."

msgid "GB125_Saladin_LS_BOT_short"
msgstr "Detonator"

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_LS_BOT"
msgstr "Corrupted Cerberus"

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_LS_BOT_descr"
msgstr ""
"A medium tank with mediocre mobility, reliable frontal armor, and an "
"excellent gun."

msgid "GB24_Centurion_Mk3_LS_BOT_short"
msgstr "Corrupted"

msgid "GB80_Charioteer_LS_PLAYER"
msgstr "Charioteer"

msgid "GB80_Charioteer_LS_PLAYER_descr"
msgstr ""
"The upgraded version of the Cromwell tank. A new turret and a 20-pounder "
"83.4-mm caliber gun made this tank a potent adversary. According to "
"different sources, between 200 and 442 Cromwell tanks were converted to the "
"new Charioteer standards."

msgid "GB80_Charioteer_LS_PLAYER_short"
msgstr "Charioteer"

msgid "GB81_FV4004_LS_BOT"
msgstr "Alpha Conway"

msgid "GB81_FV4004_LS_BOT_descr"
msgstr ""
"The tank destroyer prototype was created on the basis of the Centurion "
"medium tank. Developed for use in combat against heavy tanks of that period,"
" including the IS-3."

msgid "GB81_FV4004_LS_BOT_short"
msgstr "Alpha"

msgid "GB83_FV4005_LS_BOT"
msgstr "Alpha FV4005"

msgid "GB83_FV4005_LS_BOT_descr"
msgstr ""
"This tank destroyer project was developed on the basis of the Centurion Mk3 "
"tank in the early 1950s. The vehicle was initially tested with a mechanized "
"ammo rack. However, the ammo rack did not fit the turret, and it was "
"canceled. One prototype was manufactured and underwent trials, but the "
"vehicle never entered mass production."

msgid "GB83_FV4005_LS_BOT_short"
msgstr "Alpha"

